### The blog, from start to end. Run the requests in order (VS Code REST Client or the IDE's HTTP client).
### Needs: the application running (as the container of the sandbox behind http://api.localhost, or from the IDE at https://localhost:5001: change @host), the database with the migration applied
### (see docs/guides/database.md) and the Keycloak of the sandbox (http://auth.localhost:9999, realm aurorelabs).

@host = http://api.localhost
@keycloak = http://auth.localhost:9999/realms/aurorelabs/protocol/openid-connect/token
@slug = hello-world

### A token for bob (editor and admin). Use alice / alice for a reader.
# @name loginBob
POST {{keycloak}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

client_id=api-tests&grant_type=password&username=bob&password=bob

###
@bob = {{loginBob.response.body.access_token}}

# @name loginAlice
POST {{keycloak}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

client_id=api-tests&grant_type=password&username=alice&password=alice

###
@alice = {{loginAlice.response.body.access_token}}

### Each author creates the own profile first (the handle never changes)
PUT {{host}}/v1/authors/me
Authorization: Bearer {{bob}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "handle": "bob", "displayName": "Bob" }

###
PUT {{host}}/v1/authors/me
Authorization: Bearer {{alice}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "handle": "alice", "displayName": "Alice" }

### Bob writes a draft. Repeating it with the same Idempotency-Key returns the same answer; without it, the slug is taken (409).
# @name createPost
POST {{host}}/v1/posts
Authorization: Bearer {{bob}}
Idempotency-Key: create-hello-world-0001
Content-Type: application/json

{ "slug": "{{slug}}", "title": "Hello, world", "body": "The first post." }

###
@postId = {{createPost.response.body.id}}

### Alice cannot see the draft (404); Bob can
GET {{host}}/v1/posts/{{slug}}
Authorization: Bearer {{alice}}

###
GET {{host}}/v1/posts/{{slug}}
Authorization: Bearer {{bob}}

### A reader cannot write (403)
POST {{host}}/v1/posts
Authorization: Bearer {{alice}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "slug": "another-one", "title": "Not allowed", "body": "Readers do not write." }

### Publish (a second time is a 409)
POST {{host}}/v1/posts/{{postId}}/publish
Authorization: Bearer {{bob}}

### The list: a numbered page. Try ?title=hello, ?orderBy=title, ?pageSize=1&pageNumber=2, ?status=Draft
GET {{host}}/v1/posts?pageSize=5
Authorization: Bearer {{alice}}

### Alice comments
POST {{host}}/v1/posts/{{postId}}/comments
Authorization: Bearer {{alice}}
Idempotency-Key: comment-0001
Content-Type: application/json

{ "body": "Nice first post." }

### The comments as an infinite scroll: send the nextCursor of the answer back as ?cursor=
GET {{host}}/v1/posts/{{postId}}/comments?pageSize=2
Authorization: Bearer {{alice}}

### More of the same story ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Change only the title (a PATCH: what is not sent stays, and so does the slug)
PATCH {{host}}/v1/posts/{{postId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{bob}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Hello, world (edited)" }

### The list filtered and ordered by author
GET {{host}}/v1/posts?author=bob&orderBy=author:desc
Authorization: Bearer {{alice}}

### The feed: published posts as an infinite scroll. Send the nextCursor back as ?cursor=
GET {{host}}/v1/feed?pageSize=2
Authorization: Bearer {{alice}}

### Delete a comment (admins only): put the id of a comment of the list above
# DELETE {{host}}/v1/posts/{{postId}}/comments/<comment id>
# Authorization: Bearer {{bob}}

### Last, because it ends the story: only an admin deletes a post (alice gets 403)
DELETE {{host}}/v1/posts/{{postId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{bob}}
